Backport of https://github.com/sddm/sddm/pull/2204 (unmerged) to v0.21.0.

For a Wayland user session the compositor takes VT/DRM control via
logind, so the helper child must not stay VT_PROCESS owner of the
target VT across its execve: execve resets the SIGRTMAX release-signal
handler installed by handleVtSwitches(), and any VT switch arriving
before the compositor is up kills the session with the default
RT-signal disposition. Passing vt_auto=true keeps the VT in VT_AUTO
mode, matching the X11 path. Also prevents the kernel's 30s
VT_RELDISP stall on greeter handoff (sddm/sddm#2129).

diff --git a/src/helper/UserSession.cpp b/src/helper/UserSession.cpp
--- a/src/helper/UserSession.cpp
+++ b/src/helper/UserSession.cpp
@@ -228,7 +228,7 @@
                 }
             }

-            VirtualTerminal::jumpToVt(vtNumber, x11UserSession);
+            VirtualTerminal::jumpToVt(vtNumber, x11UserSession || waylandUserSession);
         }

 #ifdef Q_OS_LINUX
